      "summary": "Cardrona is open for skiing today, with 0°C, winds of 27 km/h and gusts reaching 47 km/h. A light 1 cm skiff of snow fell overnight, accompanied by strong southwesterly winds and some mountain fog. The wind is expected to ease through the day as the weather improves towards a fine afternoon. The fresh snow and cold temperatures have produced good conditions, although wind-blown pockets and thinner wind-stripped areas are expected across the mountain. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Willow’s Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are open, with Soho Express delayed. Learners Slopes, Main Basin, Captains, Big Willows, Ski Touring Access, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and Summit are open, with Soho delayed and Little Willows on hold. All 9 terrain parks are open. (Issued: --, 13 Sep) The access road is chain free, but chains must be carried and an active road hazard advisory remains in place. Carparks A and B are full, while C, The Yard, Valley View and The Pines have spaces. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 9 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
