      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with 1°C, winds of 16 km/h and gusts to 27 km/h. There was no new snow overnight or in the last 24 hours, while a full night of grooming has produced firm corduroy for the morning. The snow should soften with the sun, with the resort expecting good corn snow on sunny off-trail aspects by lunchtime. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Triple Treat, Beginner Platter, Roller Coaster, Upper Main Street, Lower Main Street, Bike Skite, Camel, Saddle Back, South Ridge, Bullet and Raffill's Run are listed, with Upper Main Street delayed. Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access are open, while Motatapu Chutes are on hold. (Issued: 8:00 am, 13 Sep) The access road is chain free, with a free shuttle from the bottom of the access road, although an active road hazard advisory remains in place. Carparks 1–3 are full, while The Neck and The Road have availability. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
